cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite it as below."
title: "notalone: a preregistered, control-gated pipeline for protocol-like modulation searches in pulsar single-pulse data"
authors:
  - family-names: Vladulescu
    given-names: Dragos Catalin
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-08-05
repository-code: "https://github.com/dragoscv/notalone"
license: MIT
keywords:
  - SETI
  - technosignatures
  - pulsars
  - single-pulse analysis
  - preregistration
  - Breakthrough Listen
abstract: >
  A hypothesis-neutral, falsifiable software experiment testing whether pulsar
  single-pulse feature streams contain repeated, protocol-like modulation not
  reproduced by fitted natural/statistical models. Seven frozen experiments on
  public Breakthrough Listen data (GBT + Parkes, 45 observations, 63,005 pulse
  folds) produced a bounded null: zero candidates survive the preregistered
  detection ladder; all Level-1 anomalies were attributed to instrumental gain
  wander by the registered control battery.
